{"2934330":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"RADIOSOL","steam_appid":2934330,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>RADIOSOL<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > is a journey through a desolate world burned by a planetary cataclysm. In search of answers, you will have to navigate through the ruins of megastructures and abandoned cities, avoiding the scorching rays of the Sun.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >RADIOSOL’s story is divided into two chapters. The first chapter is currently available in the game. The second chapter will be released later as a free update for all owners of the game.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >-Why do my eyes hurt so much?<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Only concrete mountains block the Sun. It hurts my eyes so much. Night used to fall quickly in these man-made valleys. But not now.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When did this stop?<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >-Why can’t I hear other people’s voices?<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I am the world's ear. I hear every radio station. I hear the hum of transistors, the boiling of mercury, and every rock on the visible side of the moon. But people don't talk anymore.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When did this stop?<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >-Why do I have so many limbs?<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >sagging - contraction - lengthening - emphasis<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >sagging - contraction - lengthening - emphasis<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >sagging - contraction - lengthening - emphasis<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Grove will be burned. Will I burn it?<\/p>","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>RADIOSOL<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > is a journey through a desolate world burned by a planetary cataclysm. In search of answers, you will have to navigate through the ruins of megastructures and abandoned cities, avoiding the scorching rays of the Sun.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >RADIOSOL’s story is divided into two chapters. The first chapter is currently available in the game. The second chapter will be released later as a free update for all owners of the game.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >-Why do my eyes hurt so much?<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Only concrete mountains block the Sun. It hurts my eyes so much. Night used to fall quickly in these man-made valleys. But not now.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When did this stop?<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >-Why can’t I hear other people’s voices?<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I am the world's ear. I hear every radio station. I hear the hum of transistors, the boiling of mercury, and every rock on the visible side of the moon. But people don't talk anymore.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When did this stop?<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >-Why do I have so many limbs?<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >sagging - contraction - lengthening - emphasis<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >sagging - contraction - lengthening - emphasis<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >sagging - contraction - lengthening - emphasis<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Grove will be burned. Will I burn it?<\/p>","short_description":"RADIOSOL is a journey through a desolate world burned by a planetary cataclysm. In search of answers, you will have to navigate through the ruins of megastructures and abandoned cities, avoiding the scorching rays of the Sun.","supported_languages":"English, Russian, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, French, German, Spanish - Spain","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/2934330\/header.jpg?t=1791472347","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/2934330\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=17914